          },
          "blocks": {
            "accordion_row_PpFM4J": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "1. What are the most popular types of necklaces?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_r9WyPJ": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Popular types of necklaces include chains, pendants, chokers, and statement necklaces. Chains and pendants offer a timeless, versatile look, while chokers and statement pieces provide a bold and modern style.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "custom",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_r9WyPJ"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_zGaB6G": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "2. What is the best metal for a necklace?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_U7yYp8": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>White Gold, Yellow Gold, and Silver are excellent choices for necklaces. Gold offers luxury and durability, while Silver provides an affordable yet stylish option. The best metal depends on your personal preference and skin tone.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "custom",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_U7yYp8"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_4Gmza3": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "3. How do I care for my gold and silver necklaces?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_LfazHg": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>To maintain the shine of your gold and silver necklaces, clean them regularly with a soft cloth and mild soap. Avoid exposing them to harsh chemicals, and store them in a cool, dry place to prevent tarnishing.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "custom",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_LfazHg"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_keYfk8": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "4. What length necklace should I choose?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_jDbKL3": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>The ideal necklace length depends on your personal style and the look you want to achieve. Common lengths include 16-inch chokers, 18-inch princess length, and 24-inch matinee. Consider your neckline and outfit when choosing the right length.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "custom",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_jDbKL3"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_JzWmTG": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "5. Can I wear my necklace every day?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_mmN79y": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes, many necklaces, especially simple chains and pendants, are designed for everyday wear. However, it's essential to remove them during activities like exercising or swimming to avoid damage or wear.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_mmN79y"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_CRcFPm": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "6. How do I prevent my necklace from tarnishing?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_jMJXxV": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>To prevent tarnishing, store your necklaces in a dry, cool place away from moisture and chemicals. You can also clean them periodically with a polishing cloth designed for your necklace’s metal.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
